Package: encryptor
Version: 3.0.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: mpgamer75 <mpgamer75@github.com>
Depends: bash (>= 4.4), openssl (>= 1.1.1), coreutils
Recommends: less
Suggests: git
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mpgamer75/encryptor
Description: Authenticated file encryption and X.509 toolkit built on OpenSSL
 Encryptor encrypts files with a password or for X.509 certificate holders,
 using only Bash and the OpenSSL command line.
 .
  - Self-describing ENCRYPTOR/3 container: cipher + HMAC-SHA256
    (encrypt-then-MAC), verified before any plaintext is written
  - Password mode: PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, 600,000 iterations
  - Recipient mode: random file key wrapped with CMS (RSA-OAEP or ECDH),
    multiple recipients
  - Secrets are never placed in process arguments or written to disk
  - Small PKI: identities, root CA, CSR, signing profiles with SANs, PKCS#12
  - Certificate expiry report and local security audit with JSON output
  - Interactive terminal UI and a scriptable command-line interface
  - Reads files written by Encryptor 2.x
